---
import '../design/design-aids.css';
---
<figure class="design-aid design-figure paper-surface" aria-labelledby="commit-order-title">
  <span class="plate-number">Illustration · Committing the price change</span>
  <h3 id="commit-order-title">Acknowledging a commit</h3>
  <ol class="events">
    <li><div><h4>Change the buffered page</h4><p>Memory contains the new 22.00 version. WAL records describe the change.</p></div></li>
    <li class="durable"><div><h4>Flush the WAL through the commit record</h4><p>The change records and commit record are now on persistent storage.</p></div></li>
    <li class="reply"><div><h4>Reply to the application</h4><p>The handler receives confirmation. The table file still has the earlier page with only the 20.00 version.</p></div></li>
    <li><div><h4>Write the changed table page later</h4><p>The table file now contains the 22.00 version too. If this page survives a crash intact, recovery can skip reapplying the change.</p></div></li>
  </ol>
  <figcaption>The table page can also be written earlier, even before commit, once the WAL for its changes has been flushed. To acknowledge a synchronous commit, PostgreSQL must also flush the transaction’s commit record.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .events { list-style:none; padding:0; margin:1.4rem 0 0; counter-reset:events; }
  .events li { counter-increment:events; display:grid; grid-template-columns:2rem minmax(0,1fr); gap:.8rem; margin:0; padding:0 0 1.2rem; position:relative; }
  .events li:not(:last-child)::after { content:''; position:absolute; width:1px; background:var(--color-text-secondary); left:.8rem; top:1.8rem; bottom:.25rem; }
  .events li::before { content:counter(events); font:.85rem/1.8 var(--font-mono); text-align:center; height:1.8rem; }
  .events li:last-child { padding-bottom:0; }
  .events h4 { margin:.1rem 0 .35rem; }
  .events p { font-size:.85rem; margin:0; }
  .events .durable > div { border-left:2px solid var(--teal); padding:.65rem .8rem; background:var(--paper-match); }
  .events .reply > div { border-left:2px solid var(--gold); padding:.65rem .8rem; background:var(--paper-highlight); }
</style>
